    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "\nEnjoying a peaceful cul-de-sac setting within walking distance of Castlebar Town Centre, 24 Garryduff Drive is an appealing four-bedroom detached home offering generous living space in a mature and well-established residential neighbourhood. Built in 1990, the residence extends to approximately 147.8 sq.m. (1,591 sq.ft.), complemented by an adjoining garage measuring a further 17.6 sq.m. (189 sq.ft.). Its combination of spacious accommodation, everyday convenience and scope for personalisation makes it an attractive choice for buyers seeking a long-term family home.\n\nAn attractive façade, sheltered entrance porch and private driveway create a welcoming introduction, with ample off-street parking and convenient access to the garage. The established surroundings lend a sense of maturity to the setting, while the cul-de-sac position adds to its residential appeal.\n\nInside, a spacious entrance hallway with timber flooring sets a warm and inviting tone, with a carpeted staircase leading to the first floor. Positioned to the front, the generously proportioned living room enjoys excellent natural light through large windows. A feature fireplace provides a natural focal point, complemented by built-in shelving, with ample space for comfortable seating and relaxed family gatherings.\n\nTo the rear, the kitchen and dining area provides a sociable and practical centre for everyday life. An extensive range of fitted units and work surfaces, together with integrated appliances, offers plenty of space for storage and food preparation. The adjoining dining area comfortably accommodates a family-sized table, creating a pleasant setting for everything from busy weekday breakfasts to leisurely meals with friends. A separate utility room off the kitchen adds further storage and workspace, along with access to the rear of the property. A guest bathroom completes the ground floor accommodation.\n\nThe first floor accommodates four well-proportioned bedrooms, offering flexibility for a growing family or those who require space for guests or working from home. The particularly spacious primary bedroom benefits from extensive built-in wardrobes and ample room for additional furnishings. The remaining bedrooms are bright and adaptable, while a well-appointed family bathroom provides both bath and shower facilities.\n\nWell maintained throughout, the home has a comfortable, welcoming feel, with an excellent foundation for a new owner to introduce their own decorative style. Its generous room sizes and practical layout offer lasting appeal, with opportunities to update individual spaces gradually to suit changing tastes and requirements.\n\nThe adjoining garage is a valuable addition, providing useful space for storage, household equipment or hobbies. It also offers potential for conversion, subject to the necessary permissions, should additional accommodation be desired.\n\nThe location brings together the tranquillity of an established cul-de-sac and the convenience of town living. Schools, shops, restaurants and leisure amenities are within easy reach, with Castlebar Town Centre just a short walk away, making this a particularly practical address for family life.\n\nWith a BER rating of C3, four spacious bedrooms and the benefit of an adjoining garage, 24 Garryduff Drive offers an excellent opportunity to secure a substantial detached home in an established Castlebar neighbourhood. Viewing is recommended to appreciate the space, setting and potential on offer."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Accommodation",
        "SortOrder": 1,
        "Content": "\nGround Floor - \n\n\nEntrance Hall - 2.26m x 4.42m\nwith laminate wood flooring.\n\nLiving Room - 6.17m x 4.42m\nwith built in units and open fireplace.\n\nKitchen Dining Room - 5.03m x 4.04m\nwith fully fitted kitchen units and porcelain floor tiles.\n\nUtility Room - 1.7m x 2.4m\nwith built in units and ceramic floor tiles.\n\nHallway - 2.9m x 1.55m\nwith laminate wood flooring and built in units.\n\nBathroom - 1.63m x 2.4m\nwith wc, wash hand basin, corner shower unit, heated towel rail and ceramic tiling from floor to ceiling.\n\nGarage - 2.97m x 5.9m\nwith double doors.\n\nFirst Floor - \n\n\nMaster Bedroom - 4.65m x 4.42m\nwith laminate wood flooring and fitted wardrobes.\n\nBedroom 2 - 3.33m x 4.06m\nwith laminate wood flooring.\n\nBedroom 3 - 3.02m x 2.77m\nwith built in wardrobes.\n\nBedroom 4 - 2.64m x 4.42m\nwith built in wardrobe and laminate wood flooring.\n\nBathroom - 1.96m x 2.77m\nwith wc, wash hand basin, corner shower unit, bath, heated towel rail and ceramic tiling from floor to ceiling.\n\n"
      },
